.TH "SAPI-ASYNC" "1" "2026-10-15" "sapi 1.0.0" "Salt API CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
sapi-async \- Execute a Salt module asynchronously (local_async) and return JID (or \-\-wait)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sapi sapi async <target> <function> [args...] [flags]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Execute a Salt module asynchronously (local_async) and return JID (or \-\-wait)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-async\fR
Start execution asynchronously (local_async) and return JID
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-batch\fR \fISTRING\fR
Execute in batches of specified size or percentage (e.g. '10%' or '5')
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-compound\fR
Match targets by compound expression (tgt_type=compound)
.TP
\fB\-G\fR, \fB\-\-grain\fR
Match targets by Salt grains (tgt_type=grain)
.TP
\fB\-\-grain\-pcre\fR
Match targets by Salt grains regex (tgt_type=grain_pcre)
.TP
\fB\-S\fR, \fB\-\-ipcidr\fR
Match targets by subnet/IPv4 address (tgt_type=ipcidr)
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-list\fR
Match targets as comma\-separated minion list (tgt_type=list)
.TP
\fB\-N\fR, \fB\-\-nodegroup\fR
Match targets by Salt master nodegroup (tgt_type=nodegroup)
.TP
\fB\-E\fR, \fB\-\-pcre\fR
Match targets by PCRE regular expression (tgt_type=pcre)
.TP
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-pillar\fR
Match targets by Salt pillar data (tgt_type=pillar)
.TP
\fB\-\-pillar\-pcre\fR
Match targets by Salt pillar regex (tgt_type=pillar_pcre)
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\-args\fR
Pass all positional and keyword arguments as raw strings without type coercion
.TP
\fB\-\-tgt\-type\fR \fISTRING\fR
Target matching type (glob, pcre, list, grain, grain_pcre, pillar, pillar_pcre, nodegroup, compound, ipcidr)
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-wait\fR
When running asynchronously, poll /jobs/<jid> until all minions return
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\-interval\fR \fIDURATION\fR
Polling interval when \-\-wait is enabled
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-ca\-bundle\fR \fISTRING\fR
Path to custom CA certificate bundle PEM (env: SALT_API_CA_BUNDLE)
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fISTRING\fR
Path to config.toml (default: ~/.config/sapi/config.toml)
.TP
\fB\-\-eauth\fR \fISTRING\fR
Salt external auth backend: pam, ldap, file, sharedsecret (env: SALT_API_EAUTH)
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-insecure\fR
Skip TLS certificate verification (env: SALT_API_INSECURE)
.TP
\fB\-\-mcp\fR
Start the integrated MCP server over stdio
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable ANSI color output
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fISTRING\fR
Output format: pretty, json, yaml, table (env: SALT_API_OUTPUT)
.TP
\fB\-\-password\fR \fISTRING\fR
Salt API password (env: SALT_API_PASSWORD)
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-profile\fR \fISTRING\fR
Configuration profile name (env: SALT_API_PROFILE)
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-timeout\fR \fIDURATION\fR
HTTP request timeout, e.g. 60s (env: SALT_API_TIMEOUT)
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fISTRING\fR
Explicit X\-Auth\-Token override (env: SALT_API_TOKEN)
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-url\fR \fISTRING\fR
Salt API base URL, e.g. https://salt:8000 (env: SALT_API_URL)
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fISTRING\fR
Salt API username (env: SALT_API_USER)
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.RS
  sapi async '*' state.highstate
  sapi async \-\-wait '*' state.highstate
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBsapi\fR(1)
